    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0335" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2286</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-02T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 2, 1915, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 3, 11.47 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>470. Reference in Italian Minister for Foreign Affairs’ speech to Italy’s part in
                    Albania considered here to indicate sending troops to Albania. This rumored now
                    going on.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
